  "result": "Perfect! All 184 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support:\n\n**Changes to `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM.\"\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **Updated `createInvoice` signature** to accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n2. **Added three helper functions:**\n   - `validateTerms(termsStr)` \u2014 Validates terms are one of NET14, NET30, or EOM\n   - `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` \u2014 Calculates due date based on terms\n   - `getLastDayOfMonth(dateStr)` \u2014 Helper for EOM calculation\n\n3. **Invoice now includes:**\n   - `terms` \u2014 the payment terms\n   - `dueDate` \u2014 calculated from issue date and terms\n\n**Due date calculation:**\n- **NET14**: 14 days after issue date\n- **NET30**: 30 days after issue date (default)\n- **EOM**: Last day of the issue date's month (handles leap years and month boundaries correctly)\n\n**Tests added (8 new, 184 total):**\n- Default NET30 terms calculation\n- NET14, NET30, and EOM term specifications\n- Invalid terms rejection\n- Month boundary handling (Feb 29 leap year, Feb 28 non-leap, 31-day months)\n- Year boundary crossing with NET14 and NET30\n\n**Key design:**\n- Terms default to 'NET30' for backwards compatibility\n- Due date stored as 'YYYY-MM-DD' string\n- EOM calculation correctly handles all edge cases (leap years, varying month lengths)\n- Invalid terms fail early during invoice creation\n\nAll 184 tests pass. \u2705",
